    "story": {
        "title": "The Elves and the Shoemaker",
        "content": "Once upon a time, there was a kind shoemaker who lived in a small house with his wife. They worked hard every day making shoes, but they were very poor. They didn’t have enough money to buy food, and soon they didn’t even have enough leather to make shoes.\n\nOne evening, after a long day of work, the shoemaker sighed. \"I wish we had enough money to buy more leather and make more shoes,\" he said. \"But I don’t know how we will manage.\"\n\nThat night, the shoemaker and his wife went to bed early, feeling sad. But little did they know, something magical was about to happen.\n\nWhen the shoemaker woke up the next morning, he saw something amazing! On his workbench were beautifully made shoes, shining and perfect. He couldn't believe his eyes! The shoes were ready to be sold, and the shoemaker was so happy.\n\nHe decided to sell the shoes in the market, and guess what? The shoes sold for a lot of money! The shoemaker bought more leather, hoping to make even more shoes. But that night, something even more magical happened.\n\nWhen he woke up the next morning, more shoes had been made while he was sleeping! They were just as perfect as the first pair. The shoemaker couldn’t understand who was helping him, but he was very grateful.\n\nNight after night, this continued. Every morning, the shoemaker would wake up to find more beautiful shoes made while he slept.\n\nOne evening, the shoemaker and his wife decided to stay awake and find out who was making the shoes. So, they hid behind a curtain and waited.\n\nTo their surprise, in the middle of the night, two tiny elves appeared. The elves worked quickly, sewing and stitching the shoes, and soon they were done. Then, the little elves quietly disappeared into the night.\n\nThe shoemaker was so happy! The next day, he made tiny clothes for the elves as a thank you. That night, when the elves came to help, the shoemaker and his wife gave the clothes to them.\n\nThe elves were very happy and said, “Thank you! We are so glad you gave us clothes. Now we will help you even more!”\n\nFrom that day on, the elves and the shoemaker worked together, and the shoemaker’s shop became the most famous one in the land.\n\nAnd they all lived happily ever after.",
        "moral": "Kindness and hard work are always rewarded."
    },
